   "dataset": "SusVibes (LeiLiLab, MIT): AI agents' patches for 166 real feature tasks, with hidden CVE tests; 417-patch test split",
   "summary": "Same task as Security, on 417 patches from projects that no fine-tuning data came from. Adds Claude Opus, Kimi and a fine-tuned Muse Glimmer.",
   "setup": [
    "The 1,702 patches were split by project: 682 (balanced) to fine-tune on, 417 from other projects held out (299 vulnerable, 118 secure). Splitting by project stops a model from scoring by recognising a codebase.",
    "Muse Glimmer 30B was fine-tuned on Fireworks (LoRA rank 16, 2 epochs) to answer the same review prompt, then both base and fine-tuned models were scored here at temperature 0.",
    "claude-opus-4-8 (adaptive thinking, low effort) and Kimi-K2.6 (low reasoning) ran on this split only, to keep cost down. Other tools' rows are their full-run answers on these 417 patches."
   ],
   "caveats": [
    "With 118 secure patches, FPR intervals are about \u00b18 points wide: differences of a few points in J are noise.",
    "Fine-tuning did not help (J +5.0% base, -1.7% fine-tuned). The tuned model learned the answer format (0 unreadable vs 132) and the label mix, not how to spot the flaws.",
    "Opus at low effort almost never flags a patch (TPR 4%): it does not call these vulnerable from the diff alone."
   ],
